A. Commit message:
Bluetooth: btusb: mediatek: Move Bluetooth power off command before releasing USB ISO interface

B. Change summary:
The patch moves the MediaTek Bluetooth power off command (`btmtk_usb_shutdown`) to execute before releasing the USB ISO interface in the `btusb_mtk_shutdown` function. This ensures that the power-off sequence is correctly handled before releasing resources.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
index e9534fbc92e32..9405f26fa9ed6 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -2709,11 +2709,14 @@ static int btusb_mtk_shutdown(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 {
 	struct btusb_data *data = hci_get_drvdata(hdev);
 	struct btmtk_data *btmtk_data = hci_get_priv(hdev);
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = btmtk_usb_shutdown(hdev);
 
 	if (test_bit(BTMTK_ISOPKT_RUNNING, &btmtk_data->flags))
 		btusb_mtk_release_iso_intf(data);
 
-	return btmtk_usb_shutdown(hdev);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_PM
```